<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<rss version="2.0" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><title>救生艇新闻：博客——保护人类</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/</link><description></description><lastBuildDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:36:00 GMT</lastBuildDate><generator>rfeed v1.1.1</generator><docs>https://github.com/svpino/rfeed/blob/master/README.md</docs><item><title>VEGFR2 抑制增强 STING 介导的抗肿瘤免疫</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/vegfr2-inhibition-potentiates-stingmediated-antitumor-immunity</link><description>韩等人。鉴定 VEGFR2 是 cGAMP-STING 信号传导的抑制剂。 cGAMP 刺激后，VEGFR2 被磷酸化，并通过激活和招募 AKT1 抑制 STING 激活。 VEGFR2 抑制剂 Ki8751 可缓解这种抑制并激活 NF-κB 信号传导，进一步放大 STING 反应和抗肿瘤作用。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/vegfr2-inhibition-potentiates-stingmediated-antitumor-immunity2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:35:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/vegfr2-inhibition-potentiates-stingmediated-antitumor-immunity</guid></item><item><title>口肠微生物传播特征能够对胃肠癌进行稳健、无创的诊断</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/mouthtogut-microbial-transmission-signatures-enable-robust-noninvasive-diagnosis-of-gastrointestinal-cancers</link><description>张等人。研究表明，口腔肠道微生物区室化的破坏是胃肠道癌症的特征。通过量化口腔到粪便的微生物传播，他们确定了可靠的诊断特征，可以对七个独立队列中的胃癌和结直肠癌进行准确分类，突出了基于微生物组的癌症检测的新非侵入性框架。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/mouthtogut-microbial-transmission-signatures-enable-robust-noninvasive-diagnosis-of-gastrointestinal-cancers2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:20:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/mouthtogut-microbial-transmission-signatures-enable-robust-noninvasive-diagnosis-of-gastrointestinal-cancers</guid></item><item><title>迷你大脑生长五年，像人脑一样成熟</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/mini-brains-grown-for-five-years-matured-like-human-brains</link><description>这些实验室培养的脑组织球可以帮助研究人员研究随着大脑老化而出现的一系列疾病。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/mini-brains-grown-for-five-years-matured-like-human-brains2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 04:05:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/mini-brains-grown-for-five-years-matured-like-human-brains</guid></item><item><title>科学家发现大脑扫描线索可预测痴呆症的到来</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-find-brain-scan-clue-that-may-predict-dementias-arrival</link><description>一种新的基于核磁共振成像的工具可以提供有关未来情况的线索，让家庭更清楚地了解疾病的进展。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-find-brain-scan-clue-that-may-predict-dementias-arrival2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:50:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-find-brain-scan-clue-that-may-predict-dementias-arrival</guid></item><item><title>显微镜为子宫修复提供了新的视角</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/microscopy-offers-a-new-view-into-uterine-repair</link><description>小鼠子宫内膜的惊人图像使研究人员建立了一种新的子宫内膜再生模型，其腺体参与程度比预期的要少。&lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/microscopy-offers-a-new-view-into-uterine-repair2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:35:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/microscopy-offers-a-new-view-into-uterine-repair</guid></item><item><title>免疫抑制性骨髓细胞通过膜结合 TGFβ1 依赖性机制诱导间充质样乳腺癌干细胞</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/immunosuppressive-myeloid-cells-induce-mesenchymallike-breast-cancer-stem-cells-by-a-membranebound-tgf%ce%b21dependent-mechanism</link><description>博耶、布莱耶等人。研究表明，表达 CD52 的免疫抑制性骨髓细胞可以塑造乳腺肿瘤的可塑性，超越免疫逃避。他们表明，这种骨髓亚群通过细胞接触传递膜结合的 TGF-β1，从而在管腔乳腺癌中产生间充质样癌症干细胞，而 TGF-β 阻断可以阻止这种干细胞程序。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/immunosuppressive-myeloid-cells-induce-mesenchymallike-breast-cancer-stem-cells-by-a-membranebound-tgfceb21dependent-mechanism2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:20:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/immunosuppressive-myeloid-cells-induce-mesenchymallike-breast-cancer-stem-cells-by-a-membranebound-tgf%ce%b21dependent-mechanism</guid></item><item><title>为什么博格人从未掌握扭曲无限来征服整个多元宇宙</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/why-the-borg-never-mastered-transwarp-infinity-to-conquer-the-entire-multiverse</link><description>&lt;img src="https://politepaul.com/fd/dtDF30237DhP.xml" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 03:05:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/why-the-borg-never-mastered-transwarp-infinity-to-conquer-the-entire-multiverse</guid></item><item><title>研究人员使用 IBM 量子计算机测试药物对接方法</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/researchers-use-ibm-quantum-computer-to-test-drug-docking-method</link><description>研究人员展示了一种资源高效的混合量子经典方法，用于在 IBM 量子处理器上进行分子对接。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/researchers-use-ibm-quantum-computer-to-test-drug-docking-method2.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 02:50:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/researchers-use-ibm-quantum-computer-to-test-drug-docking-method</guid></item><item><title>2019 年，德克萨斯大学奥斯汀分校和洛克希德·马丁公司开发了一种水凝胶系统，其产水量是商用太阳能蒸馏器的 12 倍。 7 年后，其 3.6 升/小时/平方米的净化率仍然是太阳能净化领域的引人注目的基准</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/in-2019-ut-austin-and-lockheed-martin-developed-a-hydrogel-system-producing-12-times-more-water-than-commercial-solar-stills-7-years-later-its-3-6-l-h-m%c2%b2-rate-remains-a-striking-benchmark-in-s</link><description>2019 年原始报告发布七年后，所报告的每平方米每小时 3.6 升仍然是了解太阳能净化研究潜力的有趣基准。这项工作的持久价值不仅仅是与商业太阳能蒸馏器的数值比较，而是其背后更广泛的原则：可以对材料进行设计，使可再生能源技术更具生产力。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/in-2019-ut-austin-and-lockheed-martin-developed-a-hydrogel-system-producing-12-times-more-water-than-commercial-solar-stills-7-years-later-its-3-6-l-h-mc2b2-rate-remains-a-striking-benchmark-in-s.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 02:35:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/in-2019-ut-austin-and-lockheed-martin-developed-a-hydrogel-system-producing-12-times-more-water-than-commercial-solar-stills-7-years-later-its-3-6-l-h-m%c2%b2-rate-remains-a-striking-benchmark-in-s</guid></item><item><title>科学家首次捕捉到对生命至关重要的反应过程中水重组的分子水平图像</title><link>https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-capture-first-molecular-level-images-of-water-reorganization-during-a-reaction-crucial-for-life</link><description>自然界中一些最重要的化学反应依赖于带负电和带正电粒子的耦合运动。这些过程在光合作用、催化和生物能量转换中发挥着核心作用，但仍然难以观察。 &lt;img src="https://lifeboat.com/blog.images/scientists-capture-first-molecular-level-images-of-water-reorganization-during-a-reaction-crucial-for-life.jpg" /&gt;由 PolitePaul 服务提供</description><pubDate>Sat, 29 Aug 2026 02:20:57 GMT</pubDate><guid isPermaLink="true">https://lifeboat.com/blog/2026/08/scientists-capture-first-molecular-level-images-of-water-reorganization-during-a-reaction-crucial-for-life</guid></item></channel></rss>